# This repository is compared BYTE FOR BYTE, so git must never rewrite a file
# on its way into or out of the working tree.
#
# `* -text` disables end-of-line conversion for everything. It is a no-op on
# Linux and macOS — nothing converts there — and on Windows it switches off the
# `core.autocrlf=true` that the GitHub runner image (and the Git for Windows
# installer, by default) sets globally.
#
# ★MEASURED, not assumed (2026-08-10, stage 7 rung 7). The Windows leg linked
# the onsgmls drop-in and ran the SGML corpus through tests/sgml/run.sh: 4 of
# 380 models. Byte probes on both sides of the comparison said the whole story
# in two lines —
#
#     got  esis:  A I D  T O K E N  D 1 \n ( D O C \n …     <- our output
#     want esis:  A I D  T O K E N  D 1 \r \n ( D O C \r \n …  <- the GOLDEN
#
# — so the parser was right and the checked-out golden had been rewritten. The
# same applies to the fixtures themselves, which is worse than a failed diff:
# an SGML parser treats a record boundary as data, so a converted doc.sgm makes
# the port answer a DIFFERENT question than the goldens were taken for. (One
# fixture already carried `doc.xml -text` for exactly this reason — the rule was
# known in the small and missing in the large.)
#
# It is deliberately repo-wide rather than scoped to tests/sgml/, because the
# same comparison runs elsewhere and each place would otherwise rediscover this:
# the seed's SHA256SUMS over the committed .ll files, the dazzle codegen
# goldens, the ESIS corpus, every `; Expected:` line read from a .scaly source.
* -text
